<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16188" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ērūca</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A caterpillar</i>, <i>cankerworm</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Col. 11, 3, 63, p. 464</span></i> Bip.;
					<i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 35</span></i> saep.; <i><span class="en">Col. 10,
				333</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 17, 24, 37, § 229</span></i>,
			but here Sillig reads uruca, q. v.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A sort of cole-wort</i>, Brassica eruca, Linn.;
				<i><span class="en">Col.
				11, 3, 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10,
				109</span></i>; <i><span class="en">372</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				19, 8, 44, § 154</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				8, 51</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 75</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vulg. Amos, 4, 9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
